<title>UK: Novorossiisk oil port reopens after weekend closure.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk oil port reopens after weekend closure.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main Black Sea oil terminal Novorossiisk was closed for more than three days up to early Monday due to wind and swell, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk, Russia's main outlet for exporting Urals crude, shut down from 0155 local time on Friday until 0425 on Monday, the source said.</p>
<p>Russia's two other Black Sea terminals Tuapse and Odessa were open on Monday, the source added. -- London newsroom, +44 171 542 8145</p>
